From: Earth1283 <josephcui921@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Nov 2077 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Wire chunk prefetch predictor

Wires org.dreeam.leaf.async.chunk.ChunkPrefetchScheduler into the
actual chunk lifecycle so async.chunk-prefetch and /leaf predictor
stats do something:

- ChunkPrefetchScheduler#maybePrefetch is now called once per player
  per tick from RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader#tick, the existing
  per-player chunk-loader tick loop. Previously it was never called
  anywhere, so the predictor was permanently idle and its stats always
  read 0.0 regardless of configuration.
- ChunkPrefetchScheduler#removePlayer is now called from
  ChunkMap#updatePlayerStatus on player removal, alongside the
  existing removePlayerFromDistanceMaps call, so tracked per-player
  heading/outstanding-request state is released on disconnect instead
  of leaking a ServerPlayer per disconnect for the life of the server.

